<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">States Reorganisation Act 1956</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1956">1956</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The States Reorganisation Act 1956 was a law of the Indian Parliament that redrew the boundaries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s states largely along linguistic lines, following the report of the States Reorganisation Commission. From 1 November 1956 it abolished the distinction between Part A, B and C states, creating 14 states and six union territories, among them enlarged states such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/states-reorganisation-act-1956.jpg" alt="States Reorganisation Act 1956" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of India · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_India.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
